      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5e89d0822aedbc56a3155d12|full_name} I am referring to using a camera as an override to the regular view. \n\nFor UI to track with a world camera you can set the Canvas as a Screen Space - Camera and use the world camera as the target.\n\nNote that when pulling tracking data for remote players it uses their Human Body bones (avatar) instead. The rate this data updates decreases when distance to the local player increases. So at a large distance the IK data is only received once per second.\n\nWe were having issues with PostLateUpdate being a frame or so behind causing a \"shaking\" effect that sickened a lot of players when overriding their view.\n\nWe found that using OnPreRender, OnPreCull, or OnRenderObject run correctly when pulling the local tracking data and translating the override camera to not cause the delayed \"shaking\" effect.\n\nWe chose to use OnRenderObject since we have other cameras in the world running at a fixed frame rate that occurs in LateUpdate (from a SendCustomEventDelayedSeconds) which caused OnPreX to be ran earlier or later than expected.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
